-- title:
--   Fontaine's fourth step for unipotent groups over mathbf Zₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbf Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly the ideal $(p)$, and which is adically complete for $(p)$. Let $\mathcal R$ be a commutative ring carrying a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over $\mathcal O$, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module of rank $p^{a}$ for some $a$, and assume the Cartier dual $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbf Z/p}(\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R,\mathbf Z/p)$, with its convolution ring structure, is local. Then there are heights $h,h'$ and two towers $(L_v)_{v}$, $(L'_v)_v$ of commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebras, free and finite over $\mathcal O$, with Hopf algebra maps $t_v\colon L_{v+1}\to L_v$, $t'_v\colon L'_{v+1}\to L'_v$, each surjective, with $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}L_v=p^{vh}$, $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}L'_v=p^{vh'}$, with $\ker t_v$ (resp. $\ker t'_v$) equal to the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker\varepsilon$ under the $p^{v}$-th convolution power of the identity, and with all base changes $\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}L_v$, $\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}L'_v$ again having local Cartier dual; moreover there are Hopf algebra maps $f_v\colon L'_v\to L_v$ with $f_u\circ t'_u=t_u\circ f_{u+1}$ for all $u$, an index $v$, a commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra $H$, free and finite over $\mathcal O$, a surjection $q\colon L_v\to H$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by $f_v(\ker\varepsilon_{L'_v})$, and a bijective $\mathbf Z/p$-Hopf algebra map $\psi\colon \mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}H\to\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R$ such that for every $n$ and every truncated Witt vector $m$ of length $n$ over $\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}H$ which is primitive (its image under the comultiplication agrees with the sum of its images under the two inclusions) and lies in Fontaine's subgroup for $H\to\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}H$ — that is, $m$ is the length-$n$ truncation of the image of a Witt vector $X$ over $H$ whose $(n-1)$-st ghost component lies in $(p^{n})$ — the induced image of $m$ under $\psi$ lies in Fontaine's subgroup for $\mathcal R\to\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R$. Only this one inclusion of Fontaine's submodules is asserted, not an equality.
--
--   This is the specialisation to residue field $\mathbf F_p$ (so $\mathcal O=\mathbf Z_p$) of Fontaine's fourth step in the classification of finite flat commutative group schemes: a unipotent finite flat group $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal R$ is realised, up to its special fibre and with its Fontaine submodule preserved, as the kernel of a morphism of unipotent $p$-divisible groups over $\mathcal O$. It feeds into [`Deformation.exists_pDivisibleTower_surjective_ker_eq_map_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual_zmodp`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_pDivisibleTower_surjective_ker_eq_map_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual_zmodp).
